# Vercel hosts the design phase only: the static frontend, nothing else.
#
# Without this, Vercel spots backend/pyproject.toml, decides this is a two-part
# app with a website and an API, and offers to deploy both with /api routed to
# the backend. That guess is wrong twice over. There is no service in backend/
# yet, only the domain model and its tests, so there would be nothing to run. And
# when the service does exist it cannot live here at all: it has to reach an
# infrared blaster on the home network, stay awake at 21:30 with nobody watching,
# and remember things between commands. It runs on the Pi.
backend/
scripts/
docs/
